# Mark generated / vendored files so GitHub collapses them in PRs
# and excludes them from language statistics.

# Package lock files
**/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true

# MkDocs build output (should not be tracked; belt-and-suspenders)
installer/docs/site/** linguist-generated=true

# Line endings. A stake listing names a commit of this repository, and a hunter's proof must build and
# fail at that commit on their own machine as it does on the arbiters', which run Linux. A checkout that
# rewrites line endings (git on Windows with core.autocrlf) changed the vendored files under
# arbiter-operator/foundry/lib, whose hashes VendoredFiles.t.sol checks, and failed the suite before any
# proof was added (verdikta-applications, tester bounty 400, 2026-11). So text is LF in every checkout,
# whatever core.autocrlf says:
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bytes that a test hashes or pins, and fixtures kept as they were received: never converted, either way.
arbiter-operator/foundry/lib/** -text
arbiter-operator/contracts/vendor/** -text
external-adapter/test-artifacts/** -text
